    "datePosted": "2026-11-09T10:32:22.000Z",
    "description": "Positive Action for Development (PAD) is an indigenous, non-governmental, non-profit, secular, and legally registered Ethiopian Civil Society Organization (Registration No. 2330). PAD is committed to promoting a just, compassionate, and inclusive society where all people can thrive. Guided by optimism, integrity, kindness, excellence, and impactful action, PAD provides effective humanitarian and development support to communities in need. Job Summary: Under the Project Coordinator's supervision, the WASH Officer will plan, design, implement, and monitor WASH hardware and software interventions in IDP sites and vulnerable host communities. The officer will ensure quality, sustainability, inclusion, and timely delivery of WASH outcomes in line with PAD policies, donor requirements, national standards, and WASH Cluster guidance. Key Duties and Responsibilities A. WASH Planning, Assessment and Design Develop Detailed Implementation Plans (DIPs) and procurement plans in line with project timelines, budgets, and donor requirements. Conduct rapid needs assessments, technical assessments, site surveys, and feasibility studies in IDP sites and host communities. Plan, design, and implement WASH interventions based on identified needs and technical standards. Prepare BOQs, cost estimates, technical specifications, drawings, and design documents. Design water supply systems, pipeline extensions, water points, springs, hand-dug wells, sanitation facilities, and other WASH infrastructure. Conduct technical assessments and designs for solar-powered water supply systems , including the Welen River Scheme in Sekota. Design inclusive and accessible WASH facilities for women, girls, children, older persons, and persons with disabilities. Construction and Contract Management Prepare tender documents, technical specifications, and procurement requests for WASH construction works. Participate in technical and financial bid evaluations and contractor selection processes. Supervise construction and rehabilitation works to ensure compliance with approved designs, BOQs, specifications, quality standards, timelines, and safety requirements. Manage and monitor WASH construction contracts and contractor performance. Verify measurements, work progress, material quality, and completed works. Prepare, review, and verify interim and final payment certificates. Identify construction challenges and provide timely technical solutions. Support testing, commissioning, completion, and handover of WASH facilities. Solar-Powered Water Supply and Electromechanical Systems Design and supervise solar-powered water supply systems. Supervise installation, testing, commissioning, and handover of solar water systems. Monitor pumps, solar panels, controllers, electrical components, storage tanks, and related electromechanical systems. Support preventive and corrective maintenance planning. Provide technical guidance to water-system operators on operation and maintenance. Hygiene, Sanitation and WASH Software Activities Coordinate hygiene and sanitation promotion activities with health workers and community structures. Support the development and dissemination of appropriate IEC/BCC materials. Facilitate community hygiene promotion and environmental cleaning campaigns in targeted IDP sites. Support sanitation improvement and safe hygiene practices at household and community levels. Integrate gender, protection, disability inclusion, accountability, and other cross-cutting considerations into WASH programming. Support distribution of WASH kits, MHM kits, and cleaning materials. Capacity Building and Community Engagement Lead and facilitate training for WASH committees, water-system operators, community structures, and relevant government counterparts. Strengthen the capacity of local WASH structures for sustainable operation and maintenance. Facilitate community consultations and participation throughout the project cycle. Support beneficiary identification, registration, verification, and community feedback processes. Promote community ownership and sustainable management of WASH facilities. Coordination and Representation Maintain close coordination with Woreda and Zonal Water Offices, Health Offices, local authorities, and other relevant government institutions. Coordinate WASH implementation with humanitarian and development partners. Participate in regional, zonal, and woreda WASH Cluster/coordination meetings. Represent PAD in relevant technical and coordination forums as assigned. Ensure harmonization of WASH interventions with government plans, cluster standards, and donor requirements. Monitoring, Reporting and Documentation Monitor progress against approved work plans, indicators, budgets, and implementation schedules. Conduct regular field monitoring and technical quality assurance. Prepare daily, weekly, and monthly WASH progress reports. Document achievements, challenges, lessons learned, recommendations, and follow-up actions. Maintain complete technical documentation, including assessment reports, designs, BOQs, site reports, measurement sheets, payment certificates, completion certificates, and handover documents. Support collection and management of project data using KoboToolbox and other digital platforms. Quality Assurance, Accountability and Compliance Ensure that all WASH interventions comply with approved technical designs, national standards, donor requirements, and organizational procedures. Ensure appropriate occupational health and safety measures at construction sites. Monitor the quality and appropriate use of construction materials and resources. Promote value for money and cost-effective implementation. Ensure WASH interventions are inclusive, sustainable, environmentally responsible, and responsive to community needs. Identify implementation risks and take appropriate corrective actions. Procurement and Resource Management Develop WASH-related procurement plans and technical procurement requirements. Prepare specifications and quantities for WASH materials, equipment, and services. Support procurement processes and technical evaluations. Monitor utilization of WASH resources against approved budgets. Support timely procurement and delivery of materials to project sites.",
