    "description": "VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT Opportunities Industrialization Centers – Ethiopia (OIC-E) Addis Ababa, Ethiopia Job Title: Social Worker Duty Station: Addis Ababa, Ethiopia Duration: One (1) year with possibility of extension, subject to funding and performance Reports to: Program Manager Organization: Opportunities Industrialization Centers – Ethiopia (OIC-E) Position Summary: OIC-E is seeking a committed Social Worker to carry the protection and child protection caseload in Addis Ababa. The post holder will identify and register people on the move who need protection support, manage individual cases from assessment through to closure, and lead the day-to-day work of family tracing and reunification for unaccompanied and separated children. This is a frontline role working directly with children and adults who have experienced difficult journeys. The ideal candidate is a skilled caseworker who can build trust quickly, keep accurate and confidential records, and work alongside government offices, community structures and service providers to get people the support they need. Key Responsibilities: Identification and Case Management: Conduct community outreach at transit points, terminals and community structures to identify people on the move in need of protection support, working with local government and civil society partners. Register and document cases, carry out protection assessments and develop individual case plans with each client. Manage an assigned caseload through follow-up, review and case closure, keeping case files complete, accurate and confidential. Facilitate referrals to health care, legal aid, shelter, livelihoods and other essential services, and track referral outcomes to completion. Child Protection and Family Reunification: Identify, register and document unaccompanied and separated children on the move through outreach and partner referrals. Conduct best interest assessments and prepare individual care plans, including interim care arrangements for children awaiting tracing. Carry out family tracing through national, regional and cross-border referral mechanisms and verify family circumstances before reunification. Accompany and escort children during reunification travel and complete formal handover to parents or caregivers. Conduct post-reunification follow-up at three and six months and complete case closure Shelter and Direct Support: Support the running of the OIC-E temporary shelter, including intake, resident welfare and onward planning for individuals and children accommodated there. Work closely with a psychologist to ensure that clients requiring psychosocial support are promptly identified and referred internally, and seek technical guidance from relevant staff on case-related decision. Documentation and Coordination: Maintain accurate case records in OIC-E’s case management database and submit timely case updates to relevant staff. Participate in case conferences, supervision sessions and multi-sectoral referral meetings. Contribute to monthly reporting, the feedback and complaints response mechanism, and quarterly review and reflection sessions.",
