    "description": "Post Title: Internship Program. Application deadline: November 20, 2026. Duration: 6 Months. Level: Entry level (Graduate Internship). Background The Ethiopian Human Rights Defenders Centre (EHRDC) was established in December 2019 and registered in November 2020 under registration number 5220 with the FDRE Authority for Civil Society Organizations. EHRDC focuses on advocacy, capacity building, and protection of human rights defenders in Ethiopia, ensuring their safety, security, and well-being, as well as promoting evidence-based advocacy in the country. EHRDC has launched an internship program aimed at providing hands-on experience to young human rights defenders. The program seeks to engage recent graduates who are members of one of our 13 University Human Rights Clubs in Ambo, Arba Minch, Assosa, Bahir Dar, Bule Hora, Debre Markos, Gambella, Gondar, Jigjiga, Jimma, Semera, Wolaita Sodo, and Wolkite, and who are interested in the area of advocacy, research, and capacity building of Human Rights Defenders. The position provides early career exposure to civil society work and hands on exposure to the human rights field and an opportunity to build essential professional skills. Job Summary The intern will support EHRDC’s programs through research, advocacy, and program coordination. The internship will provide practical exposure to human rights work and deepen the intern’s understanding of the opportunities and challenges facing human rights defenders in Ethiopia. The intern will conduct desk reviews, compile and organize data, prepare summaries, contribute to reports and other documents, and assist with daily program activities and event organization. Key Responsibilities The interns will assist in the following activities: Research and Documentation: The intern will assist with basic research by conducting desk reviews, compiling data, drafting short summaries, and helping prepare small sections of reports. They will also help maintain organized digital and physical documentation. Program and Activity Support: assist in organizing workshops, meetings, and training sessions, preparing materials, supporting smooth implementation, and helping prepare short activity summaries. Advocacy and Communications Support: support advocacy and communication tasks, including gathering information, preparing content for social media, and helping draft materials under supervision. The intern will also monitor and relay relevant human rights updates to the team. Monitoring and Evaluation : Assisting in monitoring the progress of program activities, including gathering data and preparing evaluation reports. Learning Opportunities for the Intern During the internship, the intern will have the opportunity to: Gain practical experience in human rights and civil society work. Learn how protection, advocacy, and capacity-building programs are implemented. Develop professional skills in communication, research, event coordination, and teamwork. Engage with HRDs, civil society partners, and relevant stakeholders. Receive mentorship and supervision from EHRDC staff and advisors.",
